    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "which follows a $ \\chi^{2} $ distribution with one degree of freedom. This is also known as McNemar's test (Sokal and Rohlf, 1995). A number of related tests have also been proposed, and Schaid and Sommer (1994) provide a nice overview of their properties.",
      "source_page": 435,
      "printed_page": 415,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter14:p043:b6"
      ],
